# Build context filter for builds that use the REPO ROOT as their context — today
# that is examples/Dockerfile (the six-role smoke test), which needs only
# certs/ca.crt. The per-service images build from their own directories
# (./pkgcache, ./webui, ./webui/console) and are unaffected by this file.
#
# Two reasons this file is not optional:
#   1. Size — caches/ is the cache tree itself (can be hundreds of GB) and
#      shuttle/ stages air-gap exports. Without these lines `docker build .`
#      uploads the entire cache to the daemon.
#   2. Secrets — private keys, .env and the control-plane stores must never
#      enter a build context, even if no Dockerfile COPYs them.

# ---- the cache state (its own git + DVC repo) and air-gap staging -----------
caches/
shuttle/
lockwarm/
dvcstore/
*.bundle

# ---- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# certs/ca.crt is public and IS needed by the example build — everything else in
# certs/ is a private key or CA serial state and stays on the host.
certs/*.key
certs/*.srl
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/users.json
config/htpasswd
config/projects.json

# ---- build/scratch output --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.venv-*/
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- docs and local working files ------------------------------------------
docs/
handoff/
handoffs/
design_handoff_checkpoint_transfer/
demo/
engineering-conventions/
*.md
inde2x.html
